   "source": [
    "# Quiz: Defining Data\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-03-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which of these could be quantitative data?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Photos of dogs</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Photos are not numbers you can measure or use in math.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Hotel reviews</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Reviews are opinions, like video comments. That makes them qualitative data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Student’s marks or grades</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Marks are numbers you can measure and use in math, so they are quantitative.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-03-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which of these could be qualitative data?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>List of employees' salaries</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Salaries are numbers you can measure and use in math, so they are quantitative.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Hotel reviews</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Reviews are opinions about the quality of something, like video comments.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Students' marks or grades</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Marks are numbers you can measure and use in math, so they are quantitative.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-03-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is the main goal of classifying data?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>To store the data correctly</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The main goal is to organize data so people and tools can understand and analyze it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>To give the data a proper name</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The goal is to organize data so people and tools can understand and analyze it, not to name it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>To know which method is best to organize it for readability and analysis</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Data must be organized so people, and the tools they use, can understand and analyze it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-03-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>The teacher is reviewing students’ number of correct answers, what type of data is that?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Qualitative Data</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A count of correct answers is a number you can use in math, so it is quantitative.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Quantitative Data</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. A count of correct answers is numerical, so it is quantitative data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>All the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A count of correct answers is used in math, so it is quantitative, not qualitative.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-03-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>A company is collecting surveys from their customers to improve their products. What type of data source is this?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Primary</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. The company collects the data itself, so it is primary data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Secondary</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Secondary data comes from someone else who collected it. Here the company collects it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Tertiary</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Data you collect yourself, like these surveys, is primary data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-03-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>A student is collecting data using queries. What data source could that be?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Local Files</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Files, like spreadsheets, are a data source, but queries are commands for databases.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>API</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. APIs share data over the internet. Queries are the commands used with databases.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Database</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Queries are commands people use to explore data in a database.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
 ],
